      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "If $f(x)=-3x-5$ and $g(x)=-5x+12,$ then $(f-g)(x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "The notation $(f-g)(x)$ means the difference of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x).$\n\nTo find the difference of the two functions, we subtract $g(x)$ from $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f-g)(x) & =f(x)-g(x) \\\\  & =(-3x-5)-(-5x+12) \\\\  & =(-3x-(-5x))-(5+12) \\\\  & =2x-17\\end{aligned}\n$$",
